# Snowflake SQL conventions

## Layout

- Pair files: `create_<name>.sql` + `update_<name>.sql`; register both in `table_configs.py`
- Migrations: `queries/migrations/*.sql` — alphabetical, **idempotent** (`ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS`, etc.)
- Ad-hoc / scratch / validation SQL: put under `queries/test_queries/` only (gitignored). Never leave one-off test `.sql` files in `queries/` root or they risk being committed with pipeline SQL
- Prefer fully qualified names: `CURRENT_DEV.DATA.<TABLE>`, `LUMINATE_PROD[_WMGONLY].EXTRACT_S.<view>`

## Patterns used here

- Prefer `MERGE INTO ... USING (...)` for incremental loads
- Snowflake does **not** support `WHEN NOT MATCHED BY SOURCE`; use a separate `DELETE ... WHERE NOT EXISTS` before the MERGE when tables must stay 1:1 with source. For large CTE sources, `CREATE OR REPLACE TEMPORARY TABLE … AS` then DELETE+MERGE against that temp (avoids duplicating the USING body). `update_tables()` splits update SQL on `;` like migrations — never put `;` inside `--` comments
- Albums (`update_marketshare_weekly_albums.sql`): keep `{checkpoint_date}` for fact MERGE only; always follow with a path-remap **MERGE** (not `UPDATE...FROM` temp) that refreshes L1/L2/L3 from current `MAP_ICPNS` (majority vote per MRELG, deterministic BU_ID tie-break) so hierarchy moves update all weeks without a full Luminate fact rebuild. Do **not** orphan-delete albums against the checkpointed MERGE source (that would wipe pre-checkpoint history)
- Artists (`update_marketshare_weekly_artists.sql`): same date/checkpoint pattern as albums (`{checkpoint_date}`, `yearid >= 2024`, incomplete-week cut). Source is MR/MP × maps, **not** an albums rollup. Grain / MERGE key is `artist_id, country_code, week_ending_date, is_current, level_1/2/3_distributor_bu_id` (SUM metrics to that path; two owners on the same path become one row). Coalesce L1/L2/L3 names and BU_IDs to `'N/A'` at map read. Follow fact MERGE with a **display-only** name remap on the existing path BU_IDs — do **not** rewrite path BU_ID key columns. `OWNER_BU_ID` is an attribute, not identity. This path PK is **inconsistent** with maps (`owner_bu_id`) and weekly/YTD/forecasts (`label_name`); **future:** key artists on `owner_bu_id` (or align all fact tables on a BU identity) so path can remap in place like albums on `mrelg_id`. Do **not** orphan-delete artists against the checkpointed fact source. Duplicate-only DELETEs on the path PK are allowed; never `TRUNCATE` / wipe the table
- Date availability: join `vw_date_ds` and often exclude the last ~2 days of incomplete data
- Placeholders: `{placeholder}` (table verify), `{checkpoint_date}` (YYYY-MM-DD) — only where Python substitutes them
- Filter market-share facts by `COUNTRY_CODE` and `WEEK_ID` for performance (Luminate cluster keys)

## Luminate columns

Do not guess Luminate field names. Use https://docs.luminatedata.com/docs/market-share (and https://docs.luminatedata.com/llms.txt for related views). Match existing casing in joins (`owner_bu_id`, `week_id`, etc.) to the surrounding file.
